      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <float.h>\n\n/* Max-heap for top-k nearest neighbors */\nstatic void heap_sift_down(float *distances, char *labels, int k, int idx) {\n    int largest = idx;\n    while (1) {\n        int left  = 2 * idx + 1;\n        int right = 2 * idx + 2;\n        if (left < k && distances[left] > distances[largest]) largest = left;\n        if (right < k && distances[right] > distances[largest]) largest = right;\n        if (largest == idx) break;\n        float tmp_d = distances[idx];\n        char  tmp_l = labels[idx];\n        distances[idx] = distances[largest];\n        labels[idx]    = labels[largest];\n        distances[largest] = tmp_d;\n        labels[largest]    = tmp_l;\n        idx = largest;\n    }\n}\n\nstatic void heap_sift_up(float *distances, char *labels, int idx) {\n    while (idx > 0) {\n        int parent = (idx - 1) / 2;\n        if (distances[idx] <= distances[parent]) break;\n        float tmp_d = distances[idx];\n        char  tmp_l = labels[idx];\n        distances[idx] = distances[parent];\n        labels[idx]    = labels[parent];\n        distances[parent] = tmp_d;\n        labels[parent]    = tmp_l;\n        idx = parent;\n    }\n}\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group *groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    /* Count total points */\n    int total_points = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) total_points += groups[i].length;\n\n    /* Allocate interleaved coordinates array and labels array */\n    float *coords = (float *)malloc(sizeof(float) * 2 * total_points);\n    char  *labels = (char  *)malloc(sizeof(char)  * total_points);\n\n    int idx = 0;\n    for (int g = 0; g < n_groups; g++) {\n        Group grp = groups[g];\n        for (int p = 0; p < grp.length; p++) {\n            coords[2*idx]   = grp.points[p].x;\n            coords[2*idx+1] = grp.points[p].y;\n            labels[idx]     = grp.label;\n            idx++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    /* Max-heap for top-k distances and labels */\n    float *heap_dist = (float *)malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\n    char  *heap_lab  = (char  *)malloc(sizeof(char)  * k);\n    int heap_size = 0;\n\n    /* Initialize with sentinel values */\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        heap_dist[i] = FLT_MAX;\n        heap_lab[i]  = -1;\n    }\n\n    /* Process each point: compute distance and maintain top-k via max-heap */\n    for (int i = 0; i < total_points; i++) {\n        float dx = to_evaluate.x - coords[2*i];\n        float dy = to_evaluate.y - coords[2*i+1];\n        float d = dx*dx + dy*dy;\n\n        if (heap_size < k) {\n            heap_dist[heap_size] = d;\n            heap_lab[heap_size]  = labels[i];\n            heap_sift_up(heap_dist, heap_lab, heap_size);\n            heap_size++;\n        } else if (d < heap_dist[0]) {\n            heap_dist[0] = d;\n            heap_lab[0]  = labels[i];\n            heap_sift_down(heap_dist, heap_lab, k, 0);\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(coords);\n    free(labels);\n\n    /* Count frequencies of labels in the heap */\n    int freq[256] = {0};\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        if (heap_lab[i] != -1) {\n            freq[(unsigned char)heap_lab[i]]++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(heap_dist);\n    free(heap_lab);\n\n    /* Find most frequent label */\n    int best_count = 0;\n    char best_label = -1;\n    for (int c = 32; c < 127; c++) {\n        if (freq[c] > best_count) {\n            best_count = freq[c];\n            best_label = (char)c;\n        }\n    }\n\n    return best_label;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n\n    Group *groups = (Group *)malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Interleaving x and y coordinates into a single array improves spatial locality by keeping both coordinates of each point adjacent in memory, reducing TLB misses and improving cache line utilization. This change builds on the previous flattening to SoA layout.",
  "notes": "Replaced separate xs/ys arrays with an interleaved coords array (float[2*total_points]) so that x and y for a given point are stored consecutively, enhancing prefetching and reducing cache misses during distance computation. Labels remain in a separate char array.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Interleave x and y coordinates into a single coords array instead of two separate arrays",
    "Adjust distance computation to use coords[2*i] and coords[2*i+1]"
